  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-143789",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "If $X$ is a discrete random variable with probability mass function $f(x)$ and sample space $S,$ the expected value of ${X}^{3}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[{X}^{3}]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}{x}^{3}\\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nSumming up the products of each cubed value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{3}] & ={\\sum }_{x\\in S}{x}^{3}\\cdot f(x) \\\\  & ={0}^{3}\\cdot \\frac{5}{18}+{1}^{3}\\cdot \\frac{2}{9}+{2}^{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =0\\cdot \\frac{5}{18}+1\\cdot \\frac{2}{9}+8\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =0+\\frac{2}{9}+4 \\\\  & =\\frac{38}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
